  "question": "A ball is projected at an angle of 45° with velocity 20 m/s. Find its range.",
  "gold_answer": "# Solved Numerical\n\n---\n\n## Projectile Tracking\n\n### Problem\nA ball is projected at an angle of $45^\\circ$ with a velocity of $20 \\text{ m/s}$. Find its horizontal range.\n\n### Given\n* Initial launch velocity ($u$) = $20 \\text{ m/s}$\n* Projection angle ($\\theta$) = $45^\\circ$\n* Acceleration due to gravity ($g$) = $9.8 \\text{ m/s}^2$\n\n### Formula\n$$R = \\frac{u^2 \\sin(2\\theta)}{g}$$\n\n### Substitution\n$$R = \\frac{(20)^2 \\times \\sin(2 \\times 45^\\circ)}{9.8}$$\n\n### Calculation\n$$R = \\frac{400 \\times \\sin(90^\\circ)}{9.8}$$\n\nSince $\\sin(90^\\circ) = 1$:\n$$R = \\frac{400 \\times 1}{9.8}$$\n\n$$R = 40.82 \\text{ m}$$\n\n### Final Answer\n**Horizontal Range ($R$) = $40.82 \\text{ m}$**\n\n### Interpretation\nThis means the ball travels a total horizontal ground shortcut distance of $40.82 \\text{ meters}$ away from its initial launch spot before striking the earth baseline.",
  "candidate_response": "┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Problem Analysis                                               │\n│                                                               │\n│ A projectile motion problem where we need to calculate the    │\n│ horizontal distance (Range) covered by a ball launched at a   │\n│ specific angle and velocity.                                  │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Given Parameters                                               │\n│                                                               │\n│ ┌─────────────────────┬───────────────────┐                  │\n│ │ Quantity            │ Value             │                  │\n│ ├─────────────────────┼───────────────────┤                  │\n│ │ Initial Velocity (u)│ 20 m/s            │                  │\n│ │ Angle (θ)           │ 45°               │                  │\n│ │ Gravity (g)         │ 9.8 m/s²          │                  │\n│ └─────────────────────┴───────────────────┘                  │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Main Formula                                                   │\n│                                                               │\n│                                                               │\n│      $$ R = \\frac{u^2 \\sin(2\\theta)}{g} $$                    │\n│                                                               │\n│                                                               │\n│ [ Explain Formula ]       [ Open Formula Lab ]                │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Step-by-Step Calculation                                      │\n│                                                               │\n│ 1. Identify the components:                                   │\n│    - $u = 20$ m/s                                             │\n│    - $\\theta = 45^\\circ$                                      │\n│                                                               │\n│ 2. Determine $\\sin(2\\theta)$:                                 │\n│    - Since $\\theta = 45^\\circ$, $2\\theta = 90^\\circ$.         │\n│    - $\\sin(90^\\circ) = 1$                                     │\n│                                                               │\n│ 3. Substitute values into the formula:                        │\n│    $$ R = \\frac{(20)^2 \\times 1}{9.8} $$                      │\n│                                                               │\n│ 4. Simplify:                                                  │\n│    $$ R = \\frac{400}{9.8} $$                                  │\n│    $$ R \\approx 40.816 \\text{ m} $$                           │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Final Answer                                                  │\n│                                                               │\n│ The horizontal range of the ball is approximately **40.82 m**.│\n│ (Note: If using $g = 10$ m/s², the range is exactly 40 m).    │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n```json\n{\n  \"formulaLabData\": [\n    {\n      \"formula\": \"R = \\\\frac{u^2 \\\\sin(2\\\\theta)}{g}\",\n      \"title\": \"Range of Projectile\",\n      \"surroundingContext\": \"Used to find the horizontal distance traveled by a projectile.\",\n      \"variables\": [\n        { \"symbol\": \"R\", \"meaning\": \"Range\", \"unit\": \"meters\" },\n        { \"symbol\": \"u\", \"meaning\": \"Initial Velocity\", \"unit\": \"m/s\" },\n        { \"symbol\": \"θ\", \"meaning\": \"Launch Angle\", \"unit\": \"degrees\" },\n        